1. Revenue & User Acquisition
    Dynamic Tiering: Implement "Telemetry Tiers" where higher-paid levels record higher-frequency data or additional channels.
    Micro-Transaction Access: "Skill-Up" pass: $5 for unlimited Pro features until specific performance benchmarks are met. how to not get played with this ?
    Referral Loop: "Analyze 5 sessions, get 2 weeks of Pro free" automated reward trigger.

2. Database & Edge Cases
    Missing Metadata Handler: Logic for when a Track/Car/Game is not in the DB (fallback to generic "Unknown" profiles with user-input prompts).
    Cleanup Service: Python CRON task to purge orphaned sessions or truncated 100+ lap stints that exceed storage quotas.

3. Social & Competitive Architecture
    Organizations: Support for "Teams" with shared telemetry folders and role-based access.
    Tournaments: Integrated leaderboard system based on verified session uploads.
    Live Review: Multi-person WebSocket sync in the Dashboard for real-time stint coaching.

4. Intelligence Engine (The ML Pipeline)
    Level 1 (Feature Extraction): Telemetry fed to a local ML model to generate a "Driver Score."
    Level 2 (Diagnostic): Identify specific faults (e.g., "Braking too early 60% of the time").
    Level 3 (Prescriptive): Generate physical targets (e.g., "Hold 80% pressure for 20% longer").
    Level 4 (Natural Language): Feed metrics to an LLM to output human-readable coaching tips in the UI.

5. Infrastructure & DevEx
    GitHub CDN: Use GitHub Actions/Repo as a lightweight CDN for distributing developer notes and app updates.
    Landing Page: Dedicated "Saved Sessions" showcase for marketing the dashboard's UI/UX.